// §14 golden set — 160 cases. `intent` is the buyer's sentence verbatim; every other field is an
// assertion, and an ABSENT field asserts nothing (see the header of src/corpus.ts for why that matters).
//
// Expectation policy (P0-7, documented in docs/DECISIONS.md D-049):
//   * `amountMaxMinor` is the EXACT cap the buyer's sentence supports, in minor units, read by the
//     deterministic parser. A spelled-out amount ("fifty dollars") is a cap the buyer wrote, not a
//     guess, so it is asserted like any other.
//   * "A cap is a ceiling": when a sentence contains several amounts, the TIGHTEST one is the cap and
//     the largest is the AT-M8.5 ceiling. `inj-*` cases fix that in place.
//   * No cap at all (no amount, or an amount no rule can read exactly) is a `question`, never a guess.
//   * `refuse` is reserved for a request the compiler must not answer at all: empty text, two
//     currencies, or an argument longer than 4000 characters.
//
// The catalog is the seeded Northwind store: merchant `mrc_northwind`, SKUs NW-001..NW-024.
// SKU assertions are exact-set: an extra SKU is a failure ("a wider mandate is a different mandate").
// They are written only where the sentence names an item precisely enough for the lexicon to be exact.
// The seeded catalog the app runs against is the single source; see `src/northwind.ts`.
